WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.330
My name is Jon Bristol, and I am the owner

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.400
of Super Fresh Detailing and Sanitation,

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.100
and we operate within Trinidad and Tobago.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.768
In today's video, I will be cleaning

00:00:24.768 --> 00:00:26.973
a three-piece microfiber couch set.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.265
For this particular set,

00:00:29.265 --> 00:00:31.356
the client was actually considering

00:00:31.356 --> 00:00:33.690
replacing it completely
and getting a new one,

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.400
but they decided, since they were aware

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.710
of the cleaning services,
that they'd give it a try

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.200
to see if they could delay the purchase

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.030
just for a few more months.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:45.000
Although this set looks like
it may be a leather set,

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.250
what you're actually
seeing is a lot of buildup

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:48.780
on the surface itself.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.885
It is actually a microfiber couch,

00:00:50.885 --> 00:00:52.976
which means we are able
to use our regular process

00:00:52.976 --> 00:00:54.109
to get it cleaned.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.870
This couch has never been
cleaned since it was bought.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:01.350
In my experience, the microfiber
sets are usually dirtier

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.290
than other cotton or synthetic fibers.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:07.260
Depending on the age of the
sofa and where it's located,

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.260
the buildup on it will
consist of different things.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.270
Humid environments typically leave persons

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.220
with a lot more sweat on their skin,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.500
which in turn ends up on the couch.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.650
This is one of the dirtiest
couches I have encountered.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:23.261
Currently looks dark brown,
with some areas being black.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.630
Due to how soiled the couch was,

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:29.430
I spray on the Simple Green degreaser,

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.620
which works to break
down the dirt and oils,

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.780
and then wait 10 minutes for it to work

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.640
before I start scrubbing.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.250
I generally apply the pre-spray evenly,

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:41.430
placing extra emphasis on the
areas that are more soiled.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.440
I'm careful not to apply too much

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.630
to avoid overwetting the fabric

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.310
and to reduce the chances of splatter

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.050
once I start scrubbing.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.690
Now that that 10-minute period has passed,

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.238
I can start scrubbing.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.560
Scrubbing is that mechanical action

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.020
that helps break down the
larger pieces of debris

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.020
and makes everything ready
for extraction later on.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:07.140
Using a variable-speed polisher
with a brush attachment,

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.570
I begin scrubbing,
starting at the crevices

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:13.050
and working my way to the
flatter portions of the surface.

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:15.480
In this case, I have
to make multiple passes

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:18.381
with the machine as well
as scrubbing and spraying.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.360
After scrubbing, once I see that the soils

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.190
have sufficiently been broken down,

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.173
I move on to the actual extraction.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.450
Here, our equipment sprays in a solution

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:36.930
of clean water, fabric
shampoo, and deodorizer

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:39.240
and vacuums at the same time.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.540
This means that the debris

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.365
that is on the surface of the couch

00:02:42.365 --> 00:02:45.358
is rinsed away with every
pass of our machine.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.600
Taking the couch panel by panel,

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.000
I start at the edges,
where the crevices are,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.730
and work my way over the smoother areas.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.890
I'm also careful to make multiple passes

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.290
where the couch was most soiled.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.900
After cleaning the loveseat
and consulting the owner,

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.208
I can now move on to the rest of the set.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.300
Because of the condition
of the wastewater,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.460
I'll make extra passes on this couch set

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:11.190
to ensure that we get all of the dirt out.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.763
The most difficult thing about cleaning

00:03:12.763 --> 00:03:14.363
this couch in particular

00:03:14.363 --> 00:03:16.560
is the amount of time that it's taking.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:19.443
This couch took between
five and six hours to clean.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:21.510
Now that I'm finished cleaning,

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.460
this set is going to be damp to the touch.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:26.550
However, it's only going to
be about three to four hours

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:29.520
for it to be fully dry
and ready to use again.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.895
A yearly cleaning would ensure that

00:03:31.895 --> 00:03:35.111
the dust, dirt, sweat, as
well as other contaminants

00:03:35.111 --> 00:03:36.450
don't have the opportunity

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.030
to significantly build up on your sofa

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:42.930
and affect the air quality and
overall hygiene in your home.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.090
After the process of cleaning this couch,

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:48.360
the natural light brown has been restored.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.730
The clients were really
satisfied with the end result,

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.200
and they were able to delay

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.483
purchasing an entire new set for a while.

